  "authored_scope": "Random mode builds a tree of dotted walks on a spacing-2 lattice with random parity. The trunk starts at the checker, branches leave at junctions, and every walk ends at a ring. One leaf is the target: its root chain is coloured c, and all departures from it use other colours. Sub-branches may keep or change colour. An optional extra non-c walk leaves the target toward another box. Background, checker colours, path colour and distinct ring colour pairs are all random. Sides are 14..30 (default 16..30); sizes other than 22x22 are synthetic extensions. Not supported: dots on the outermost border rows/columns, diagonal paths, more than one checker, and dots of mixed lattice parity. Explicit mode replays the fixtures from latent boxes, segments and target, and rejects partial, mistyped or ambiguous scenes.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Exactly one checker box. All other boxes are rings with outer != centre, and box colours differ from the background.",
    "Box tops are at Chebyshev distance >= 4, so boxes never touch.",
    "Exactly one dot touches the checker box's 12 edge cells.",
    "c-coloured dots form one connected chain from the checker to the target only. No c dot touches any other ring box.",
    "Each ring box is touched only by the last dot of the walk ending there (plus the extra walk's first dot at the target).",
    "Dots are lattice-adjacent (distance 2) only to their tree parent and children. All dots share one (row%2, col%2) parity.",
    "The only background-free 3x3 windows are the declared boxes.",
    "Ring (outer, centre) pairs are distinct within a scene.",
    "At least one colour-changing branch leaves the c path in every scene.",
    "Integer-only controls: booleans and floats are rejected."
  ],
  "semantic_review": {
    "status": "reviewed",
    "checks": [
      "Four canonical pairs exact and1000 independent seeds20000..20999 agree with archived solver.",
      "Independent solid-box detector plus union-find connectivity verifies1693 scenes, including1000 defaults,400 targeted cases,all289 supported shapes andfour canonical pairs.",
      "1024 scenes contain disconnected path-colour dots touching a distractor ring; every such scene still has exactly one start-connected target. Default sample has480/1000 such cases.",
      "All1693 scenes have a colour-change decision;89 match path colour to a checker colour,407 have an extra non-main walk from the target andallfour lattice parities occur.",
      "Forced same-colour decoys work on every supported14..30 shape;50 minimum14x14 calls need at mostfour construction attempts.",
      "Added explicit disconnected_decoy control and post-construction label/window checks that surface bugs rather than silently filtering.10 malformed/infeasible controls reject.",
      "1000 independent seeds 20000..20999; approved validation fixtures reconstructed exactly; canonical replay reported separately"
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Default scenes attempt a disconnected same-colour tail with probability0.5; guaranteed examples require disconnected_decoy=True. This is a labelled synthetic extension.",
      "Geometry remains a spaced tree of dotted orthogonal walks, optionally with a non-main walk from the target. No arbitrary cyclic graph coverage.",
      "Checker colour may equal path colour, a labelled synthetic extension handled by explicit box detection.",
      "Ring count, walk length and extra-target-walk occurrence remain sampled, not exact user controls.",
      "Explicit replay permits broader reference-consistent layouts; requested sizes14..30 beyond22 are synthetic scale extensions."
    ]
